+// BibleText patch: type every character but a control. A keyboard's string
+// arrives here one character at a time (app.keyboardTyped), and stock Fyne
+// kept only what strconv.IsPrint accepts. That dropped the zero-width joiner
+// and non-joiner with every other format character, every space but U+0020,
+// private-use characters and characters newer than Go's Unicode tables: a
+// joined emoji was typed as separate emoji, and Persian and Indic text lost
+// its joiners. The rule is now the desktop driver's, GLFW's _glfwInputChar:
+// C0 controls, DEL and C1 controls are dropped, and so is a value that is not
+// a character (the Android key path gives -1 for a key with none, and sets
+// the sign bit for a dead key). Everything else is typed, and what a field
+// keeps is the application's to decide, as it is on the desktop.
